/// always; `lotNo` is populated ONLY when unambiguous — see drying_batch_multi_lot's finding text in
/// domain/dataQuality/checks.ts for the exact rule and the 22 rows it excludes (11 comma/slash-
/// joined like "387, 401", 11 numerically concatenated 6-digit values like 246253, both genuinely
/// unsplittable). A THIRD, separate contamination is also real here and reported separately
/// (drying_batch_lot_column_holds_bin_code): 41 of the 138 rows hold a bin code
/// ("BIN-03B"/"BIN-005"/"BIN-007"/"BIN-015"/"BIN-016") in lotNoRaw, not a lot number at all — lotNo
