  /// ever populated there), and Postgres treats every NULL as distinct in a unique index — a
  /// warehouseSite-keyed constraint would never catch a re-uploaded central row as a duplicate.
  /// `warehouse` (the store/site value the sheet actually always fills) does the same
  /// per-site-sequence job `sn` alone can't (sn restarts at 1 for BOUAKE after ANAGROCI-01 hits 81).
  @@unique([warehouse, sn])
  @@index([lotNo])
  @@index([ficheNoRaw])
  @@index([warehouseSite])
